{
  "version": "2026-10-25.1",
  "status": "draft: pending review by the project owner (approved in principle on 2026-10-25)",
  "scope": "Top allergen codes from decision A-08. Not medical advice; cross-contamination is not modelled.",
  "how_it_is_used": [
    "keywords: any ingredient whose normalized name contains a keyword (whole-word match) gets that allergen flag. Keywords only ADD flags; they never make a recipe's allergen data complete.",
    "keyword_exceptions: phrases that contain a keyword but are not that allergen (e.g. coconut milk is not dairy).",
    "known: single foods whose allergen codes are known. A recipe is allergen-complete only if EVERY ingredient matches a 'known' entry exactly. Composite or variable products (bread, pasta, stock, sauces, spice blends, chocolate, vegetable oil) are deliberately absent, so recipes using them stay 'unknown' and are excluded for users with allergen exclusions."
